WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.189 --> 00:00:03.390
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.120
- [Narrator] Line up the top
seven US carriers by size

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.670
and this is how it looks today.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:13.470
But JetBlue's $3.8 billion
deal to buy Spirit Airlines

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.333
last month would change this picture.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.530
The tie-up would see
Spirit folded into JetBlue

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.040
moving JetBlue one rung
up the ladder past Alaska.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.960
- You know, the word they've
used is turbochargers

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.250
and that's probably right that, you know,

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.510
if they're able to get this deal done,

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:28.343
it really puts them

00:00:28.343 --> 00:00:29.940
in a different class really quickly.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.560
- [Narrator] But the so-called Big Four,

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.744
American, United, Delta and Southwest,

00:00:33.744 --> 00:00:36.090
would maintain their places.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.680
- If you look at what this is

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.110
it's really an acquisition about assets.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:45.110
It's about JetBlue acquiring
Spirit for aircraft

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.270
and for the crew members, who
will operate those aircraft.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:49.350
- [Narrator] The question is

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.260
can a bigger JetBlue compete and how?

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.090
Let's take a look at a few key metrics

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:56.160
to see where the company stands now,

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.110
where it will be if the deal goes through,

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:00.243
and if there could be a Big Five?

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.823
First, pilots.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.570
Anyone who's been to an airport recently

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.150
knows that travel is rough right now.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.950
One of the challenges
airlines have started

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.510
to grapple with this summer,

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.430
there aren't enough pilots.

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:16.680
Globally, demand for pilots is projected

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.750
to exceed supply by 2024.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.940
But in North America, it's already here

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.830
and airlines are scrambling to both hire

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.990
and retain employees.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:28.320
- You've seen carriers
like Spirit, Frontier,

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.970
Allegiant, JetBlue lose
pilots who's choosing to go

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:35.970
to United, American, Delta, Southwest.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:39.570
And so this is really a way
for JetBlue to basically

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:44.570
acquire a cadre of pilots
to really fuel that growth.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.620
- [Narrator] By adding
Spirit, JetBlue would jump

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:50.550
from having around 3,800
pilots to nearly 6,600.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.170
That's still about half of Delta's

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.590
industry-leading 13,180 pilots.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:58.470
- Having more pilots it just
gives them a lot more depth.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.261
And so when they go into a new market,

00:02:00.261 --> 00:02:02.010
they can offer multiple flights a day

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.750
instead of maybe just one, or they can go

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:04.890
into more new markets,

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.750
where they're not already present.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.610
And you know that just
makes them potentially

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.146
more meaningful competitor.

00:02:10.146 --> 00:02:11.910
- [Narrator] JetBlue would also benefit

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:14.310
from the type of pilots the deal brings.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:17.520
JetBlue and Spirit, both
fly mostly Airbus aircraft.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.730
- To have pilots who
are already a type rated

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.789
and qualified to fly an Airbus A320

00:02:23.789 --> 00:02:27.750
or an A321 simplifies things

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.660
and really reduces cost for a JetBlue.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.490
- [Narrator] Next up fleet.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:36.600
Without its deal for Spirit,
JetBlue has a total of 282 jets

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.600
in its fleet putting it
well behind the Big Four.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.360
- Getting planes it's just
difficult for airlines right now.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.300
There's delays in deliveries,
manufacturing delays.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:48.450
So just the idea of just quickly acquiring

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:51.690
a couple hundred planes was
very enticing for JetBlue.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.820
- So acquiring Spirit's all Airbus fleet

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.780
would give JetBlue a total
of 458 planes JetBlue says,

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.000
with some 300 more on order.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.500
- That would take it many years,

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.450
I think they've said eight
years, to sort of get

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.210
to that size that they
need to get organically.

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.880
So they kind of looked around and deciding

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.100
really the best way to
kind of jump to a size

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.250
that can even begin to compete
with these bigger airlines

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.050
is through an acquisition.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.300
- [Narrator] These planes
won't fly as is though.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.160
Spirit's yellow will be painted over

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.320
and JetBlue has said
it would take seats off

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.360
Spirit's packed planes
to bring them in line

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.370
with JetBlue's roomier model,

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.742
but even taking seats away,

00:03:27.742 --> 00:03:31.560
this deal would bring JetBlue
thousands more seats total.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.750
So let's talk about seats.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.550
To see how the airline stacks up,

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:39.210
it's best to look at a metric
known as available seat miles.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.220
This metric is calculated by multiplying

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.440
the number of seats
available on a given flight

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:46.214
by the number of miles
that plane will travel.

00:03:46.214 --> 00:03:48.930
- The more ASMs you have,
the more capacity you have.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.741
So it's a great metric to show the size

00:03:51.741 --> 00:03:54.570
from a capacity standpoint of an airline.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:57.480
- [Narrator] In 2021,
JetBlue had 54 billion

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:58.890
available seat miles.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.780
Combining with Spirit's 40 billion

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.600
would edge the airline closer
to fourth place Southwest,

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.550
then sixth place, Alaska.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.530
But even with Spirit, JetBlue's slice

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.500
of overall seat capacity will sit at 8%.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.030
Analysts say to grow that,

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:14.250
JetBlue will need to expand its reach.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:17.220
- I think what really
is needed for JetBlue

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:21.750
to get its share closer
to that of Southwest,

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:24.180
United, Delta, and America is to set up

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:27.810
some sort of a focus
city with material size

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.220
in the middle of the country.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:31.560
- [Narrator] And lastly destinations.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:34.980
Currently, JetBlue flies
to 98 destinations.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.630
Spirit flies to 90.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:40.170
The combined airline
wouldn't fly to 188 however.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:43.770
That number is more like
127, according to JetBlue.

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:46.020
- Often in airline mergers
in the past, you know

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:48.300
regulators say, well,
this is where you overlap.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:52.800
We need you to cut
certain gates at airports

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.684
or need you to divest
some assets in order to,

00:04:55.684 --> 00:04:57.270
so there's not so much overlap.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:58.590
If the deal is allowed to go forward

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:01.080
there will likely be
some pruning at least.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:05.340
- 127 destinations would move
JetBlue just above Southwest,

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:08.670
which currently flies to 121 locations.

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:10.350
The other three would all have more

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:12.174
than double JetBlue's destinations.

00:05:12.174 --> 00:05:13.410
(plane whooshing)

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:14.940
The deal would make Fort Lauderdale

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:18.480
JetBlue's busiest airport
according to a Cirium analysis.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.430
The combined airline would then surpass

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:23.160
Southwest and Delta to become
Florida's second busiest

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:25.380
carrier by seats after American.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.900
- Florida has been, especially
the last couple of years

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:32.280
just one of the busiest
places in the country to fly.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.540
It is important to airlines

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.040
to have a meaningful presence there

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.400
and growing there can be
really advantageous for them.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.590
- [Narrator] JetBlue says
it's larger presence in cities

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:43.710
like Ford Lauderdale, would
drive down prices for flyers.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.920
However, JetBlue would be
taking an ultra low cost carrier

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.120
out of the equation.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.760
And some argue that less
competition could end up

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:52.770
raising prices for all.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:55.110
Proving that competition
and low prices will remain

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:56.520
after the deal will be key

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:59.160
to getting regulators to bless the merger.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:05:59.993
- JetBlue has argued

00:05:59.993 --> 00:06:02.670
that the government has
allowed the creation

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:05.280
of four really big airlines
that dominate the market

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.900
by allowing all of these mergers.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:10.170
And that the only way to
address that situation

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:13.320
is to allow another
carrier to kind of bulk up

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:16.020
and get big enough to challenge
those four big airlines.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.120
- [Narrator] Spirit and
former suitor Frontier,

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:19.290
had previously argued

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:21.930
that regulators would almost
certainly prevent a merger

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:23.430
between Spirit and JetBlue

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:25.560
and that the review
process could hobble spirit

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.120
for up to two years.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.770
JetBlue has said that any deal,

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:30.330
including the failed combination

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:33.060
between Spirit and Frontier
would face similar levels

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.800
of pushback from regulators.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.960
JetBlue expects the
deal to receive approval

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:39.930
and be finalized by the first half of 2024

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:42.900
followed by a four to five
year integration process.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.120
And analysts say an even longer time

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:47.523
before it might truly
challenge the Big Four.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.640
- It won't be five years from now.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.220
Won't be 10 years from
now, but I think what this

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:57.510
does is create a combined
airline that becomes competitive

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:58.830
with those Big Four

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:02.070
and really makes the future JetBlue

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:03.838
relevant in the industry.

00:07:03.838 --> 00:07:06.505
(gentle music)

